  "articleBody": "Getting interior trim installed correctly elevates an entire room, but choosing the right finish contractor requires knowing what goes into the work. Trim ties your flooring, drywall, and doors together, meaning it requires tight precision.\n\nKey Benefits\nUpgrading your baseboards, casing, and interior trim adds sharp definition, protects lower walls from daily wear, and creates crisp transitions between rooms. Quality trim work also increases the finished feel and visual value of your home.\n\nProcess Breakdown\nThe job begins with precise measuring of every wall and opening, calculating roughly 15 to 20 percent extra for cuts and waste. Next, raw wood trim must acclimate indoors for at least 48 hours to match household humidity. After surface preparation, your contractor cuts, copes, fits, and securely fastens pieces into wall studs before filling nail holes, caulking joints, and applying finish paint or stain.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process\nIn real homes around the Denver area, walls and subfloors are rarely perfectly flat. A skilled finish carpenter inspects how baseboards align with your finished flooring height and ensures pieces are anchored to framing rather than merely biting into drywall.\n\nGet Started\nWhen you are ready to update your interior woodwork, contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your project scope.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
